From: Charles Hoskinson <charles.hoskinson@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:34:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] T7c: path C on the universal L key

stmt: the root statement of L takes an N3 child (full tree) or a
leaf-layer child (path C, pc = 1). On path C it receives the 62 leaf
words and the child pre-hash, requires h_pre = 0, outputs the SEG of
the leaf, and sends the DAG key leaf P2(DOM_KEYDAG, entry, PATH_C,
enc(X), h_pre, pre_app, cc_app) (I-17: the child pre-hash joins the
leaf). KeyPathAir proves the leaf in key_root (KR_BUS 970);
RootSealAir opens prog_d to key_root on path C. On the full tree X is
the key constant x_n3. X is a root statement word (FP-3 words 74 to
106 move from the Stmt interface AIR to the root statement AIR).

lverify: Gen::cached_in records the L cached commitments. t7_chain:
the universal L (child-meta, fixed heights over both children), L_Fr
with the L commitment as input and the X check, the pathc and shape
modes; fp8_d3 takes the path C leaf layer at the internal set.
