+/// The seal of `L` (X10 and FP-3 fact 1 check (i)): receives `(prog_d, post_d, pc, key_root)`,
+/// opens `post_d` as `P2(SHK_SD2, header 41 words)`, checks the seal predicates (a terminal
+/// `outcome_tag`, `deps_d = EMPTY_DEPS`; SEG and `h_lo = 0` are fixed by the root statement),
+/// and exposes the three `R` operand digests (24 public values after the FP-3 table). T7c, path
+/// C: opens `prog_d = P2(DOM_PROG, image_d, plan_d, key_root, machine_version)` (the first node
+/// does this on the full tree) and receives the `key_root` that [`KeyPathAir`] reaches.
